<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Former Yan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">337–370</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Former Yan was a state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-xianbei">Murong</a> clan in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, proclaimed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-huang">Murong Huang</a> in 337 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixteen-kingdoms">Sixteen Kingdoms</a> period. In 342 it sacked the Goguryeo capital and carried off the queen mother and the body of the previous king. It later conquered much of northern China and moved its capital to Ye, before falling to Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in 370.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/former-yan.jpg" alt="Former Yan" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sixteen_Kingdoms_338_AD_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
